release: 2026.10.12
resolution: Implemented and merged in #1 (fcf34e5).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #1 as fcf34e5; checks successful at head 3161974: CodeQL, codeql, test (22), test (26)."
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:58:34.300Z",pi-glm-transport,"Plan: implement src/github.ts as the single typed GitHub boundary (createGitHubTransport with injectable fetch/token/env/gh reader/pageSize/timeout; fixed GraphQL endpoint, redirect:error, AbortSignal timeout; REST only for the paginated legacy commit-status list). snapshot() pages review threads (nested replies+reactions), submitted reviews, issue comments, commits, check suites (nested runs) and statuses; fail closed on malformed data, missing/repeated/cycling cursors and mid-snapshot head changes; final head re-check after all pages. Real read-only fixtures for public PR unbraind/pm-rl#68 recorded via gh at small page size so every connection paginates; synthetic fixtures cover >100 nodes, all failure paths, mutations (synthetic transport only, never against the real PR) and token resolution. Schema fields verified live: ReviewThread.path/line/isResolved, PullRequestReviewComment.originalCommit, PullRequestReview.commit/url/createdAt, mutation inputs addPullRequestReviewThreadReply(pullRequestReviewThreadId), addReaction(subjectId), resolveReviewThread(threadId)."
  "2026-10-12T11:20:47.405Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator verified the worker draft and adopted final ownership for corrections. Public fixture refresh records 84 read-only requests at head 14669bcf58229e7226eed958470babc06c88d570, with credentials and request headers excluded. Nested query page size is bounded, each continuation is consumed once, malformed/cycling pages fail closed, and newer runs win per app and check name. Transport tests pass 29/29; mutation tests use synthetic responses only."
  "2026-10-12T11:24:05.856Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: resetting the continuation cursor inside drain makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pages every connection\" test/github.test.ts fail. Restored byte-for-byte. The regression paginates 150 nodes in every supported connection, including nested replies/reactions/runs."
  "2026-10-12T11:45:48.101Z",codex-sol,"Refreshed the complete 84-request public fixture with an unfiltered visible-reviews query, so pending review objects cannot disappear from round evidence. The public head and inventory remain unchanged. Valid WAITING and REQUESTED check states are normalized to pending."
  "2026-10-12T12:01:17.104Z",codex-sol,"Corrected the synthetic write wire contract: GraphQL variables must be thread/body for ReplyThread, node/content for React, and thread for ResolveThread. Synthetic fetch assertions now require those exact maps. The focused mutation test passes; restoring the old reply binding alone makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"thread mutations\" test/github.test.ts fail. Restored correct bindings before gates. No mutation went to GitHub."
  "2026-10-12T13:22:59.548Z",codex-sol,"Node 22 CI has 61 passes and 8 cancellations: the timeout test has no referenced event-loop handle. Hold and clear a referenced timer in its synthetic fetch, with no production change."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:33.364Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463348 / Node 22 CI: synthetic stuck fetch now holds a referenced timer and clears it on abort. Node 22.23.1: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"bounds every request\" test/github.test.ts passes 1/1. Reverting only the referenced handle cancels the test with Promise resolution still pending and exits 1. Production transport unchanged."
